{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_5","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"rg -n 'p7b|ticks' collab --glob '*brief*'\"","aggregated_output":"collab/general/1790523957004-architect-shibi-cap-vs-currency-brief.gpt-6-sol.stdout.log:24:{\"type\":\"item.completed\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_11\",\"type\":\"command_execution\",\"command\":\"/bin/zsh -lc \\\"sed -n '185,225p' docs/design/yin.repl.link-policy.md\\\"\",\"aggregated_output\":\"\\n### 6.2 What the option carries\\n\\n```text\\n:link-policy {:lease {:duration {:seconds 30}\\n                      :tolerance {:seconds 2}\\n                      :max {:seconds 300}        ; optional cap\\n                      :ticks tick-source}}       ; host adapter\\n```\\n\\nUnits are the composition's interoperability decision, fixed once. The\\nsizing relations of `dao.lease.md` hold: the duration exceeds twice the\\nrenewal interval, and the tolerance covers flight time and the rate skew\\nbetween the judge's and the holder's tick streams.\\n\\n### 6.3 Attribution comes by construction\\n\\n`dao.lease.md` makes attribution a composition duty, and warns that\\nin-process media distinguish no writers unless the composition arranges it.\\nHere it can be arranged completely: the lease media and the tick streams\\nare the shell's own, per-author, and never placed in a VM's private\\n`:resources` or handed to any program value. A program holds only sealed\\nreferences to resources the engine issued, so it cannot append a forged\\ngrant or renewal. The resolver is therefore the shell's own knowledge of\\nwhich medium each author writes. A capability token such as ShiBi is not\\nneeded for this case and would add nothing until leases guard something\\nthat untrusted writers can reach.\\n\\n### 6.4 What phase 2 costs\\n\\n- a tick adapter per host (a timer on the JVM, on Node and on Dart), which\\n  is the one place a host clock is read, outside the REPL core;\\n- a judge, driven at a declared cadence by the same host driver that\\n  drives the shell;\\n- lease bookkeeping that survives the rollbacks M5 fixed: the lease for a\\n  link is reclaimed by the same abandon path, and a link identity is never\\n  reused on the surviving pair;\\n- scripted-tick tests, as `dao.lease`'s own tests are: no test reads a\\n  real clock;\\n- process-scoped leases only. The judge's ledger is not rebuildable from\\n  any stream and the resource is not durable, so a restart drops the\\n\",\"exit_code\":0,\"status\":\"completed\"}}\ncollab/dao-stream/1790497500000-architect-pending-link-policy-brief.gpt-6-sol.stdout.log:9:{\"type\":\"item.completed\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_2\",\"type\":\"command_execution\",\"command\":\"/bin/zsh -lc \\\"rg -n -C 8 'pending|lease|deadline|expire|timeout' docs/design/dao.lease.md\\\"\",\"aggregated_output\":\"1-# DaoLease\\n2-\\n3:Status: implemented (`src/cljc/dao/lease.cljc`, `test/dao/lease_test.cljc`,\\n4:`test/dao/lease_composition_test.cljc`; merged 2026-09-20), derived from and\\n5-subordinate to [`datom.world.md`](./datom.world.md). The three use cases in\\n6:[`dao.lease.implementation-plan.md`](./dao.lease.implementation-plan.md) are\\n7-sketches, not finished components. This document is the operative contract:\\n8-every sentence below is a rule. Why the design is this shape is in\\n9:[`dao.lease.rationale.md`](./dao.lease.rationale.md), which binds nothing.\\n10-\\n11:A lease is a grant that lapses unless renewed. It adds no operation to any\\n12-contract and no key to any DaoStream result map, leaving\\n13-[`dao.stream.md`](./dao.stream.md) unchanged by its existence.\\n14-\\n15-## Vocabulary\\n16-\\n17-Facts are plain data on ordinary streams, classified by two dispatch keys:\\n18:`:dao.lease/status` for the negotiation, `:dao.lease/event` for evidence. A\\n19:reader switches on both. A fact carrying neither is not a lease fact and is\\n20-ignored; a fact carrying both is defective.\\n21-\\n22-+----------+-----------------------+---------+---------------------------------------------+---------------------------------------------------------------------------+\\n23:| Fact     | `:dao.lease/status`   | Author  | Identity carried                            | Also required                                                             |\\n24-+==========+=======================+=========+=============================================+===========================================================================+\\n25:| Proposal | `:dao.lease/proposed` | holder  | `:dao.lease/proposal`                       | `:dao.lease/subject`; `:dao.lease/duration` optional, an ask              |\\n26-+----------+-----------------------+---------+---------------------------------------------+---------------------------------------------------------------------------+\\n27:| Grant    | `:dao.lease/accepted` | grantor | `:dao.lease/lease`, plus                    | `:dao.lease/subject`, `:dao.lease/holder`, `:dao.lease/duration`;         |\\n28:|          |                       |         | `:dao.lease/proposal` if answering one      | `:dao.lease/max` optional                                                 |\\n29-+----------+-----------------------+---------+---------------------------------------------+---------------------------------------------------------------------------+\\n30:| Refusal  | `:dao.lease/rejected` | grantor | `:dao.lease/proposal`                       | —                                                                         |\\n31-+----------+-----------------------+---------+---------------------------------------------+---------------------------------------------------------------------------+\\n32:| Release  | `:dao.lease/released` | holder  | `:dao.lease/lease`                          | —                                                                         |\\n33-+----------+-----------------------+---------+---------------------------------------------+---------------------------------------------------------------------------+\\n34:| Reclaim  | `:dao.lease/lapsed`   | grantor | `:dao.lease/lease`                          | `:dao.lease/cause` — `:silence`, `:release`, `:cap`, or `:policy`         |\\n35-+----------+-----------------------+---------+---------------------------------------------+---------------------------------------------------------------------------+\\n36-\\n37-+------------+----------------------+---------+----------------------+----------------------+\\n38:| Evidence   | `:dao.lease/event`   | Author  | Identity carried     | Also required        |\\n39-+============+======================+=========+======================+======================+\\n40:| Renewal    | `:dao.lease/renewal` | holder  | `:dao.lease/lease`   | —                    |\\n41-+------------+----------------------+---------+----------------------+----------------------+\\n42:| Tick       | `:dao.lease/tick`    | adapter | —                    | `:dao.lease/reading` |\\n43-+------------+----------------------+---------+----------------------+----------------------+\\n44-\\n45-**Keys.**\\n46-\\n47:- `:dao.lease/lease` — the lease's identity, minted by the grantor, carried by\\n48-  every fact about it, never reused within that grantor.\\n49:- `:dao.lease/proposal` — a proposal's identity, minted by the holder, echoed\\n50-  by the grant or refusal answering it.\\n51:- `:dao.lease/subject` — what is leased, in whatever plain data the domain uses.\\n52:- `:dao.lease/holder` — the party whose renewals count, in whatever form the\\n53-  medium's attribution takes.\\n54:- `:dao.lease/duration` — a single-entry map from a unit keyword to a positive\\n55:  integer magnitude. `:dao.lease/max`, `:dao.lease/reading` and a judge's\\n56-  tolerance use the same representation; tolerance may be zero. A magnitude\\n57-  stays within the bound that keeps every comparison and sum of the\\n58-  composition's units exact on every host — the reference bound is 2^52 raw\\n59-  and, against a supplied table, `quot 2^52 unit-magnitude`; a magnitude past\\n60-  it establishes nothing.\\n61:- `:dao.lease/cause` — why a reclaim happened.\\n62-\\n63-**Units.** The unit keywords and their ratios are a composition's\\n64-interoperability decision, fixed once and shared by its grantor, holders and\\n65-judge. Comparison normalizes to the finer of two units, and is strict: an\\n66-interval exactly equal to its bound has not yet passed it.\\n67-\\n68-**Validity.** A fact is defective, and establishes nothing, when it omits a key\\n69-its status or event requires; carries a status or event outside the tables\\n70-above; carries a duration, cap or reading that is not a single-entry map of a\\n71:fixed unit to a positive integer; carries a lease id on a proposal; answers one\\n72-proposal with both `:accepted` and `:rejected`, or repeats `:accepted`,\\n73:`:released` or `:lapsed` for one lease; or carries a reading older than one\\n74:already observed. A judge reading a defective fact has read no lease fact.\\n75-\\n76-## Authority\\n77-\\n78-- **Only grantor-authored facts establish terms.** A holder cannot grant itself\\n79-  tenure. A holder fact establishes no term; a delayed holder renewal is still\\n80-  evidence and counts as such.\\n81:- **A renewal counts only when its attributed author is the lease's holder.**\\n82-  A renewal from any other author is a fact about that author, and silence is\\n83-  measured as though it had not arrived.\\n84-- **At most one of `:accepted` or `:rejected` answers a proposal.**\\n85-  Renegotiating is a new proposal with a new proposal identity.\\n86-- **A proposal creates no state.** Nothing exists until `:accepted`. A grantor\\n87-  owes no answer, and a holder's wait on an unanswered proposal is bounded by\\n88-  nothing in this vocabulary.\\n89-- **A grantor may grant unsolicited**, with no proposal, in which case the\\n90-  holder is the party the grant is delivered to.\\n91-- **A `:policy` cause may not consist of declining to count evidence\\n92-  received.** Eligible renewals are counted whether or not another condition\\n93:  ends the lease.\\n94-\\n95-## Prohibitions\\n96-\\n97:- A lease may not extend retention, defer eviction, or gate history, and no\\n98:  DaoStream operation may consult a lease.\\n99-- No timer holds a callback and no notification marks a lapse.\\n100-- No absolute time appears in any fact.\\n101-- A reclaim frees the resource, never the record.\\n102-- A holder renews from its own control flow. No machinery renews on its behalf.\\n103-\\n104-## Time\\n105-\\n106:Time reaches lease code only as data; neither judge nor holder reads a host\\n107-clock. Both read a tick stream their composition wires. Readings on one stream\\n108-never decrease, and a composition persisting a ledger across a restart keeps\\n109-its readings comparable across it.\\n110-\\n111:A tick-stream gap makes a pass late, not wrong; a lease-fact gap is governed\\n112-under *Judging with incomplete evidence*.\\n113-\\n114-## The judge\\n115-\\n116-The judge is composed **inside the boundary that possesses the resource** and\\n117-reclaims by acting on what it itself holds; one that does not possess the\\n118-resource is outside this contract. It concludes and reclaims in one\\n119-interpreter, which is not the forbidden collapse: it is the possessing host\\n120-interpreter performing its own act.\\n121-\\n122:**Ledger.** The judge keeps, privately, for each live lease:\\n123-\\n124-- its **terms** — subject, holder, duration, cap;\\n125-- its **tenure start**, the reading the grant was seeded at, which no renewal\\n126-  changes;\\n127-- its **last relevant observation**, the reading of the grant or newest\\n128-  eligible renewal, whichever is later;\\n129-- its **evidence state** — `known`, or `unknown` with its resumed reading;\\n130:- its **reclaim state** — `live`, or `pending` carrying the classified cause\\n131-  and whether the reclaim succeeded.\\n132-\\n133:A lease **enters** the ledger when the grantor grants it, seeded from that act,\\n134-and **leaves** once its reclaim has succeeded and its `:lapsed` record has been\\n135-appended with `:dao.stream/ok`. Until both, it remains.\\n136-\\n137-The ledger is not rebuildable from any stream: a composition either persists it,\\n138-as a stream its owner writes and reads, or recovers by the rule under *Restart*.\\n139-\\n140-### The pass\\n141-\\n142-A pass classifies nothing until a first tick has been observed. At each pass,\\n143-in this order:\\n144-\\n145-1. **Drain every wired tick cursor** to `:dao.stream/blocked`. The newest\\n146-   reading drained, or the newest previously observed if none were drained, is\\n147-   **now** for the whole pass.\\n148:2. **Drain every wired lease-fact cursor** to `:dao.stream/blocked`, stamping\\n149-   each fact with that same *now*, and apply it: an eligible renewal advances\\n150:   the lease's last relevant observation to *now* and returns it to `known`; a\\n151:   valid `:released` from the holder marks it released; a `:dao.stream/gap`\\n152:   marks every lease on that medium `unknown` with *now* as its resumed\\n153-   reading. Each cursor's drain may be bounded by a composition-declared\\n154-   budget; a cursor still yielding when the budget is spent has not completed\\n155-   its observation, and while any wired fact cursor is so truncated, the pass\\n156:   classifies no `:silence` for the leases that truncated medium carries —\\n157:   `:release`, `:cap`, `:policy` and pending retries are never suppressed. An\\n158-   incomplete drain may delay a reclaim; it may never manufacture one.\\n159-3. **Answer and grant.** Proposals drained this pass may be answered, and\\n160-   unsolicited grants authored, both seeded and stamped with this pass's *now*.\\n161-   A grant authored between passes is seeded with the next pass's *now*.\\n162:4. **Classify.** A lease is due for reclaim when any of these holds, and the\\n163:   first that holds in this order is its cause: it is already `pending`, and\\n164:   keeps the cause it carries; a valid `:released` from its holder has been\\n165:   observed, `:release`; its tenure start is further back than\\n166:   `:dao.lease/max`, `:cap`; the grantor's own policy ends it, `:policy`; its\\n167-   interval since the last relevant observation exceeds duration plus\\n168:   tolerance, `:silence`. A lease whose evidence state is `unknown` is due for\\n169-   `:silence` only once, in addition, a full duration has passed since its\\n170-   resumed reading.\\n171:5. **Reclaim** each due lease by its composition-supplied procedure, marking it\\n172:   `pending` with its cause first. The procedure is idempotent and reports\\n173-   whether it succeeded; a reclaim that fails or does not report leaves the\\n174:   lease `pending` and unrecorded.\\n175:6. **Record** `:lapsed`, carrying the cause the ledger holds, for each lease\\n176:   whose reclaim succeeded. On `:dao.stream/ok` the lease leaves the ledger;\\n177:   otherwise it stays `pending` and the next pass reaches it again through the\\n178-   first clause of step 4.\\n179-\\n180-The record follows the act and never precedes it. **The absence of a `:lapsed`\\n181-fact is never evidence of tenure.**\\n182-\\n183-A drain that ends in `:dao.stream/end` retires that cursor for subsequent\\n184-passes. A drain that ends in `:dao.stream/transport-error` ends the pass before\\n185-step 4.\\n186-\\n187-### Judging with incomplete evidence\\n188-\\n189-Absence is evidence only over a window the judge observed. After a\\n190:`:dao.stream/gap`, a lease with no renewal in the retained tail is `unknown`,\\n191:and a surviving older renewal is not inferred to be the newest. A lease\\n192-recovered from a persisted ledger is `unknown`. Conditions other than\\n193:`:silence` apply to an `unknown` lease unchanged.\\n194-\\n195-### Restart\\n196-\\n197-A grantor that has lost its ledger **reclaims and re-grants**: for each\\n198-resource it still possesses it performs the reclaim first, then grants afresh.\\n199-The reclaim ends the prior tenure; a new grant alone does not.\\n200-\\n201-This requires an inventory of possessed resources and a recoverable holder for\\n--\\n208-  it by the same attribution its composition supplies to the judge. A holder\\n209-  that has not observed its grant holds nothing.\\n210-- **Renew at less than half the duration**, measured against ticks on its own\\n211-  tick stream. A renewal is an append returning `:dao.stream/ok`; any other\\n212-  outcome does not advance the holder's bound.\\n213-- **Stop acting at the bound** — the earlier of the duration since the later of\\n214-  its last renewal and its observed grant, and the cap the grant carries —\\n215-  whether or not anything has been heard.\\n216:- **Release when done.** The grantor still performs the reclaim and records\\n217-  it.\\n218-- **Treat an unusable reading as unanswerable.** A reading that is not a\\n219-  single-entry `{unit, positive integer magnitude}` within the composition's\\n220-  table answers nothing: every holder discipline fails closed on it, and a\\n221-  flow that guards on its bound alone does not act.\\n222-\\n223-For cap purposes, the holder measures the cap interval from the reading at\\n224-which it observed the grant; that reading may be later than the grantor\\n--\\n226-extend, delay, or alter the judge's cap or reclaim decision; a resource\\n227-requiring exclusion must enforce it through fencing.\\n228-\\n229-The bound bounds attention, not access; a holder needing exclusion obtains it\\n230-from the resource.\\n231-\\n232-## Composition duties\\n233-\\n234:A composition that grants leases owes all of the following.\\n235-\\n236-- **A judging interpreter, and a runtime driving it at a declared cadence** —\\n237-  the maximum interval between *completed* passes.\\n238-- **A tick stream** for the judge, and one for every holder.\\n239-- **A tolerance** supplied to the judge, possibly zero.\\n240-- **An attribution resolver** for the judge and for every holder observing a\\n241-  grant — its own answer to who authored a fact, by per-author media, an\\n242-  envelope key, or a transport's attachment identity, since DaoStream supplies\\n--\\n245-- **A reclaim procedure per subject**, idempotent, reporting success.\\n246-- **A stream the grantor writes grants and `:lapsed` to**, and the medium each\\n247-  recipient reads its carried facts from.\\n248-- **Media that either retain without eviction or declare evict-oldest**,\\n249-  refused at assembly otherwise.\\n250-- **For durable resources, three things this vocabulary does not supply**: a\\n251-  judge whose durability matches the resource, a rule for which incarnation may\\n252-  reclaim, and fencing from the resource. A composition that has not settled\\n253:  all three keeps its leases process-scoped.\\n254-\\n255-## Sizing\\n256-\\n257-Stated as relations; the values belong to compositions.\\n258-\\n259-- The granted duration exceeds twice the holder's renewal interval.\\n260-- The judge's tolerance covers expected flight time and the rate skew between\\n261-  its tick stream and the holder's.\\n--\\n268-\\n269-## Limits\\n270-\\n271-- **A false lapse is possible.** Delay errs against the holder while a renewal\\n272-  is unobserved and for it once observed, so a late-observed renewal from a\\n273-  dead holder buys a fresh duration, and continuity is lost when none is\\n274-  observed before a completed pass finds the interval past duration plus\\n275-  tolerance. Partition length alone decides neither.\\n276:- **`:dao.lease/max` binds within one ledger lifetime.**\\n277-- **A medium that gaps more often than one duration** never completes an\\n278-  observation window and leaks continuously while every component reports\\n279-  healthy; per-attachment media are the isolation.\\n280-- **Reclamation is bounded by** duration plus tolerance plus cadence plus the\\n281-  reclaim's own cost, given an uninterrupted observation window.\\n282-\\n283-## Carriage\\n284-\\n285:Proposals, grants, refusals, releases and renewals cross a boundary as ordinary\\n286-payload, carried by the composition to the medium the recipient reads. Carriage\\n287-is delivery, not a second authoring.\\n288-\\n289-`:lapsed` does not cross; it is the grantor's record on the grantor's stream. A\\n290-remote holder learns of a reclaim by observing it — for a served connection, an\\n291-ordinary `:ws/closed`; for a stream served under `dao.stream.remote.md`, the\\n292-`not-found` protocol error its mirror answers for the reclaimed identity. A remote holder that\\n293-reads the grantor's stream through a served handle is observing the grantor's\\n294-record, not receiving carriage. No close code is assigned here; distinguishing\\n295-reclaim on the wire belongs to `dao.stream.ws.md`'s deferred close-code design.\\n296-\\n297-## Out of scope\\n298-\\n299-- **Delegated renewal.** A renewal is evidence about its author.\\n300:- **Transfer of a lease between holders.**\\n301-- **Who may be granted anything at all**, and **what is leasable** — this\\n302-  contract gates nothing, and the domain decides. `dao.stream.remote.md`\\n303-  names two subjects: a stream entry served for a remote party, and a relay\\n304-  pair on a meeting peer.\\n\",\"exit_code\":0,\"status\":\"completed\"}}\ncollab/dao-stream/1790497500000-architect-pending-link-policy-brief.gpt-6-sol.stdout.log:18:{\"type\":\"item.completed\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_8\",\"type\":\"agent_message\",\"text\":\"Completed-GMT: 2026-09-27 08:24:44 GMT\\nCompleted-Local: 2026-09-27 15:24:44 Asia/Ho_Chi_Minh\\n\\n## Pending-link failure policy — owner decision brief\\n\\n**Decision:** Who ends a link when its content source never answers? M5 currently leaves the link pending without a deadline. At the REPL, the pending run retains subsequent input until the link completes or the caller uses `(abandon)`.\\n\\n| Option | Decision and change | Cost |\\n|---|---|---|\\n| **A — Keep the current behavior permanently** | The linker stays clock-free. A caller that wants a deadline composes `dao.lease` and calls `abandon` when its lease lapses. | No linker work now; every caller owns its timeout policy indefinitely. |\\n| **B — Add a lease per pending link now** | Wire lease grants, renewals, ticks, judging, and reclaim into linker operation. | A new dependency and lease bookkeeping for every pending link, including callers that want to wait indefinitely. |\\n| **C — Defer, with a documented composition hook** | Keep M5 behavior and identify the point where a caller’s lease judge would call `abandon`. Implement a deadline when a deployment needs one. | No lease runtime now; documentation and a later implementation decision remain. |\\n\\n**Current implementation:** M5 implements A’s *behavior*, but the owner has not chosen A as the permanent policy. The [linker design](</Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/docs/design/yin.vm.linker.md>) assigns retry, deadline, and permanent absence to the composition; `fetch` has no deadline. Its section 6.3 already describes the lease seam: the caller renews on progress, and a judge supplied with ticks calls `abandon` on silence. The [lease contract](</Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/docs/design/dao.lease.md>) requires that judge and its resource reclaim action to live in the possessing composition. A proposed [REPL link-policy design](</Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/docs/design/yin.repl.link-policy.md>) describes a configurable hook, but marks it unimplemented.\\n\\n**Recommendation: C.** Preserve the clock-free linker and document the caller-side `abandon` seam as the decision for now. This follows the existing ownership boundary and avoids imposing lease state on every link before a deployment supplies a deadline, cadence, and recovery needs. When such a deployment exists, its requirements can determine whether a caller-side lease composition suffices. The owner need only rule now that indefinite pending remains the default and that deadlines belong to the composition.\\n\\nStatus: COMPLETE\"}}\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
