{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_11","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '2270,2325p;3740,3845p;3880,3935p' src/cljc/yang/php/antlr/lower.cljc; sed -n '1,110p' test/yang/php/antlr/e2e_harness.clj; rg -n 'register_shutdown_function|shutdown-functions|php/.*builtin|php/init' src/cljc/yang/php/antlr/prelude.cljc | head -50\"","aggregated_output":"            (mapcat (fn [k] (if (p/rule? k) (texts k) [(:text k)]))\n                    (core/kids ctx x)))]\n    (app* 'php/echo (u/lit (byte-string (apply str (texts n)))))))\n\n\n(defn- contains-token?\n  \"True when a token of type `t` occurs below `n`.\"\n  [ctx n t]\n  (boolean\n    (some (fn [k] (if (p/rule? k) (contains-token? ctx k t) (= t (:type k))))\n          (core/kids ctx n))))\n\n\n(defn- with-temps\n  \"`node` followed by the release of the temporaries it registered, when the\n   statement `n` holds a call that can leave one (row 37).\"\n  [ctx n node]\n  (if (or (some #(core/contains-rule? ctx n % #{}) [\"functionCall\" \"newExpr\" \"memberAccess\"])\n          (contains-token? ctx n \"Clone\"))\n    (let [mark (core/gen \"tm\" n)]\n      (u/let1 mark (app* 'php/tmp-mark) (u/then node (app* 'php/release-tmps (u/v mark)))))\n    node))\n\n\n(defn- block-nodes\n  [ctx n]\n  (mapv #(lower ctx %) (core/rule-kids ctx n)))\n\n\n(defn- sequence-node\n  [nodes]\n  (if (seq nodes) (u/seq-nodes nodes) (u/lit :php/null)))\n\n\n;; -----------------------------------------------------------------------------\n;; Loops and escapes\n;; -----------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n(defn- loop-frame\n  \"A level of the `:loops` stack. `:used` collects the escapes the body\n   takes (`:brk`, `:cont`), so only those are bound.\"\n  [n switch?]\n  {:brk (core/gen \"brk\" n),\n   :cont (core/gen \"cont\" n),\n   :used (atom #{}),\n   :switch? switch?})\n\n\n(defn- push-frame\n  [ctx frame]\n  (update ctx :loops conj frame))\n\n\n(defn- wrap-escape\n  \"`node` under a `php/call-ec` that binds the frame's `kind` escape, when the\n   body used it.\"\n\n(defn lower-module-body\n  \"The unit's statements as one node, before the runtime wrapper: what\n   lowering goldens compare. Hoisted function declarations come first.\"\n  [packet]\n  (unit-body (context packet)))\n\n\n(def option-keys\n  \"The options `lower-program` and the lowering stage accept. Request data\n   never flows here: the harness attaches the composition-supplied request\n   stream and composes its sealed reference as `run-main`'s second operand\n   (`:request-node`, an opaque UAST node) at the composition level — the\n   record itself reaches the runtime only when `run-main` consumes it.\"\n  [:prelude :path :paths :class-map :request-node :response-node :diag-node])\n\n\n(defn- path-map-node\n  \"`(php/bind-path-map! {path thunk ...})` for the composition's published\n   paths (plan P6 R3): the computed include's lookup table.\"\n  [paths]\n  (app* 'php/bind-path-map!\n        (reduce (fn [m path] (app* 'assoc m (u/lit path) (delivery-thunk path)))\n                (u/lit {})\n                (sort paths))))\n\n\n(defn lower-program\n  \"`{:ast a :warnings [d ...]}` for one ok packet: the unit body run by\n   `php/run-main` after the prelude, tail calls marked. Its value is\n   `{:php/out s :php/diag [...] :php/uncaught nil-or-{:class :message}}`.\n   `:warnings` are the lowering's warning-severity diagnostics\n   (`:yang.php/unknown-builtin`, `:yang.php/compile-warning`,\n   `:yang.php/computed-include-path`).\n\n   Options: `:prelude` is `:bundled` (default; the prelude tree ahead of the\n   body) or `:linked` (`(require 'yang.call) (require 'php) (php/init!)`, the profile includes\n   need); `:path` the entry unit's declared path (default `entry-path`);\n   `:paths` the normalized paths whose units the composition published,\n   which a computed include resolves against; `:class-map` true requires\n   the published `phpm.$classmap` and binds its classes and delivery thunks\n   (plan P6 R9), which takes the place of `:paths`; `:request-node` is the\n  opaque `run-main` second-operand node the harness composed from the\n  attached request stream (lowering never embeds request data — `run-main`\n  consumes the record from the stream at runtime);\n  `:response-node` and `:diag-node` are the opaque third and fourth\n  operands: the composition-supplied stream references execution emits\n  on. Absent, `run-main` runs with two operands and the cells\n  accumulate.\"\n  ([packet] (lower-program packet {}))\n  ([packet {:keys [prelude paths path class-map request-node response-node diag-node],\n            :or {prelude :bundled}}]\n   (when-not (contains? #{:bundled :linked} prelude)\n     (throw (ex-info \"unknown PHP prelude profile\"\n                     {:yang.php/diagnostic :yang.php/unsupported,\n                      :construct :prelude,\n                      :prelude prelude})))\n   (let [linked? (= :linked prelude)\n         request-node (or request-node (u/sexp->uast :php/null))\n         ctx (context packet {:path (or path entry-path), :linked? linked?})\n         ;; `run-main`'s second operand arrives composed by the harness from\n         ;; the attached request stream: production initialization consumes\n         ;; the record from the stream at runtime and seeds the superglobals,\n         ;; no postwalk rewrite and no request data through lowering involved.\n         ;; With stream nodes `run-main` takes four operands (request,\n         ;; response and diagnostics references); without them it takes two\n         ;; and the cells accumulate.\n         main (if (or response-node diag-node)\n                (app* 'php/run-main (u/lam [] (unit-node ctx)) request-node\n                      (or response-node (u/sexp->uast :php/null))\n                      (or diag-node (u/sexp->uast :php/null)))\n                (app* 'php/run-main (u/lam [] (unit-node ctx)) request-node))]\n     {:ast (u/mark-tails\n             (if linked?\n               (u/seq-nodes (concat [(app* 'require (u/lit 'yang.call))\n                                     (app* 'require (u/lit prelude/module-name))\n                                     (app* 'php/init!)]\n                                    (when (and (seq paths) (not class-map)) [(path-map-node paths)])\n                                    (when class-map\n                                      [(app* 'require (u/lit classmap-module))\n                                       (app* 'php/bind-class-map!\n                                             (u/v (symbol (str classmap-module) \"classes\"))\n                                             (u/v (symbol (str classmap-module) \"paths\")))])\n                                    [main]))\n               (u/then prelude/uast main))),\n      :warnings @(:warnings ctx)})))\n\n\n(defn lower-packet\n  \"The complete program for one ok packet (`lower-program`'s `:ast`).\"\n  ([packet] (lower-packet packet {}))\n  ([packet opts] (:ast (lower-program packet opts))))\n\n\n;; =============================================================================\n;; The module emitter: one PHP unit as the linker module phpm.<mangled-path>\n;; =============================================================================\n\n(def module-exports\n  \"The exports of a compiled PHP unit: its spec and body, immutable after\n   install.\"\n  '#{spec body})\n\n\n(defn imported-unit-names\n  \"The normalized paths the unit statically includes through folded literal\n    (u/mark-tails (apply u/app (u/lam params (u/lit nil)) operands))))\n\n\n(defn module-spec\n  \"`yin.vm.linker.publish/publish-module!`'s spec for the unit at `path` over\n   the host registry `registry`, requiring `php` at `php-address` and each\n   included unit at its address in `deps` ({path address}). A free name no\n   requirement or profile supplies is refused before anything is published.\n   This namespace emits; it never publishes.\"\n  [registry packet {:keys [path strict-types php-address deps]}]\n  (core-module/module-spec\n    :yang.php/refusal :yang.php/undeclared-free registry\n    {:name (path-module-symbol path),\n     :ast (module-packet packet {:path path, :strict-types strict-types}),\n     :exports module-exports,\n     :runtime-name prelude/module-name,\n     :runtime-address php-address,\n     :deps (into {} (map (fn [[p a]] [(path-module-symbol p) a])) deps)}))\n\n\n;; =============================================================================\n;; The autoload class map (plan P6 R9)\n;; =============================================================================\n\n(def classmap-exports\n  \"The exports of the class map module: the lower-cased class name to path\n   map, and the path to delivery-thunk map the computed include resolves\n   through.\"\n  '#{classes paths})\n\n\n(defn classmap-paths\n  \"The literal paths a class map `{:classes {class path} :paths [path ...]}`\n   publishes thunks for: `:paths`, else the class map's values, and always the\n   class map's values. Normalized, sorted, distinct.\"\n  [{:keys [classes paths]}]\n  (vec (sort (distinct (map #(let [r (normalize-unit-path %)]\n                               (when (:error r) (throw (ex-info \"unmappable class map path\"\n                                                                {:yang.php/diagnostic :yang.php/unsupported,\n                                                                 :construct (:error r), :path %})))\n                               (:path r))\n                            (concat (vals classes) paths))))))\n\n\n(defn classmap-packet\n  \"The class map as one linker module (the unit module shape): `classes`\n   maps each lower-cased class name to its normalized path, `paths` each\n   listed path to its delivery thunk.\"\n  [{:keys [classes] :as cm}]\n  (let [paths (classmap-paths cm)\n        norm (fn [p] (:path (normalize-unit-path p)))\n        defs [(u/def! 'classes\n                      (u/lit (into {} (map (fn [[c p]] [(str/lower-case c) (norm p)])) classes)))\n              (u/def! 'paths\n                      (reduce (fn [m p] (app* 'assoc m (u/lit p) (delivery-thunk p)))\n                              (u/lit {})\n(ns yang.php.antlr.e2e-harness\n  \"The JVM end-to-end harness: PHP source -> CST packet -> lowering stage ->\n   program envelope -> the bundled program on each of the four VMs. Output\n   is the unit's bottom buffer, a latin-1 byte carrier, decoded as UTF-8\n   here at the boundary.\"\n  (:require\n    [dao.host.text :as text]\n    [dao.stream :as stream]\n    [yang.php.antlr.cst :as cst]\n    [yang.php.antlr.lower :as lower]\n    [yang.php.antlr.portable-harness :as portable]\n    [yang.php.antlr.safepoint :as hooks]\n    [yang.core.uast :as u]\n    [yang.safepoint :as safepoint]\n    [yin.vm :as vm]\n    [yin.vm.debruijn.register :as rvm]\n    [yin.vm.debruijn.stack :as dvm]\n    [yin.vm.encoder :as encoder]\n    [yin.vm.semantic :as semantic]\n    [yin.vm.semantic.derive :as derive]\n    [yin.vm.semantic.linearize :as sr-linearize]\n    [yin.vm.test-utils :as tu]))\n\n\n(defn host-registry\n  \"The registry the PHP compositions run over.\"\n  []\n  (portable/host-registry))\n\n\n(def ^:private base-opts\n  {:make-stream tu/make-stream,\n   :capability-secret tu/secret,\n   :primitives vm/primitives})\n\n\n(def ^:private load-semantic\n  (vm/fresh-code-loader semantic/load-ast vm/ast-contract))\n\n\n(defn request-node\n  \"The `run-main` second-operand node the composition supplies for `request`:\n   the harness converts the record to UAST itself — lowering never embeds\n   request data.\"\n  [request]\n  (u/sexp->uast (or request :php/null)))\n\n\n(defn lower-program\n  \"`{:ast a :warnings w}` for `source` through the lowering stage, or\n   `{:diagnostics d}`. Warning-severity diagnostics do not stop the program.\n  The request record travels the composition path: the harness consumes it\n  (a plain record here) and composes it as `run-main`'s second operand —\n  lowering itself never sees request data.\"\n  ([source] (lower-program source nil))\n  ([source request]\n   (let [cst-log (tu/new-memory-log)\n         program (tu/new-memory-log)\n         diagnostics (tu/new-memory-log)]\n     (stream/append! cst-log (cst/parse-source source))\n     (lower/step-stage (lower/open-stage cst-log program diagnostics\n                                         (cond-> {:medium lower/program-medium}\n                                           (some? request) (assoc :request-node\n                                                                  (request-node request)))))\n     (let [{warnings true, problems false}\n           (group-by #(= :warning (:severity %)) (tu/drain diagnostics))]\n       (if (seq problems)\n         {:diagnostics problems}\n         (let [{:yin/keys [batch root] :as envelope} (first (tu/drain program))]\n           {:ast (nth batch root), :envelope envelope, :warnings (vec warnings)}))))))\n\n\n(defn packet->form\n  \"The nested form of a CST packet, spans dropped: `[:rule child ...]` for a\n   rule, `[\\\"TYPE\\\" \\\"text\\\"]` for a token. The inverse of\n   `portable-harness/packet`.\"\n  [{:yang.cst/keys [root nodes]}]\n  (letfn [(form\n            [id]\n            (let [{:keys [kind rule type text children]} (nth nodes id)]\n              (if (= :token kind)\n                [type text]\n                (into [(keyword rule)] (map form) children))))]\n    (form root)))\n\n\n(defn latin1->text\n  \"The UTF-8 text of the byte carrier `s`.\"\n  [s]\n  (text/utf8-decode (.getBytes ^String s \"ISO-8859-1\")))\n\n\n(defn render\n  \"The text a unit prints: its output, then, for an uncaught error, the\n   fatal line (no path, plan section 3.9).\"\n  [{:php/keys [out uncaught fatal]}]\n  (str (latin1->text out)\n       (when uncaught\n         (str \"PHP Fatal error:  Uncaught \" (:class uncaught) \": \" (:message uncaught)))\n       (when fatal\n         (str \"PHP Fatal error:  \" fatal))))\n\n\n(defn run-vms\n  \"`{vm-key rendered}` of `ast` on the four VMs; a host throw is\n   `[:thrown message]`. `:execution-budget` derives the PHP safepoint hooks\n   and starts one per-run counter; no option leaves the AST unchanged.\"\n  ([registry ast] (run-vms registry ast {}))\n  ([registry ast {:keys [execution-budget envelope]}]\n   (let [ast (if (some? execution-budget)\n32:   Runtime state is allocated by `php/init!`, once per task, under the slot\n33:   `php.rt/state` (the literal `:php/uninit` until `php/init!` flips it to\n4224:    [php/init-props\n4228:           (php/init-props\n4240:                      (php/init-props (php/empty-array) (get c :props-decl) 0\n4761:                                                         :props (php/init-props (php/empty-array)\n5932:  \"The functions `php/init!` registers: PHP name to prelude definition,\n5938:  \"The lower-cased names of the functions `php/init!` registers.\"\n5943:  \"The builtin classes and interfaces `php/init!` seeds: [name kind parent\n6079:  \"`php/init!`'s body: the runtime cells, the builtins, the ready flag, under\n6146:   prelude function, the literal state slot, then `php/init!`. Defining them\n6150:         ['php/init! (init-form)]]))\n6176:   allocated by `php/init!`.\"\n6177:  (u/then functions-uast (u/sexp->uast '(php/init!))))\n6190:  \"Every key `php/init!` allocates, the ready flag aside, sorted.\"\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_12","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '3280,3315p;400,470p;3680,3740p' src/cljc/yang/php/antlr/lower.cljc; sed -n '5930,5945p;6070,6145p' src/cljc/yang/php/antlr/prelude.cljc; rg -n 'Ticks|directive|declareStatement' src --glob '*.g4'; rg -n 'site-set' src/cljc/yang/python/antlr/siteset.cljc src/cljc/yang/core/publication.cljc\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_12","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '3280,3315p;400,470p;3680,3740p' src/cljc/yang/php/antlr/lower.cljc; sed -n '5930,5945p;6070,6145p' src/cljc/yang/php/antlr/prelude.cljc; rg -n 'Ticks|directive|declareStatement' src --glob '*.g4'; rg -n 'site-set' src/cljc/yang/python/antlr/siteset.cljc src/cljc/yang/core/publication.cljc\"","aggregated_output":"   each item's `{:ns :uses}` environment keyed by its CST id. The block\n   rules of PHP are compile errors here (mixed forms, code before the first\n   namespace, code outside a braced block).\"\n  [ctx]\n  (let [root-items (mapcat (fn [k]\n                             (cond\n                               (p/rule? k \"inlineHtml\") [k]\n                               (p/rule? k \"phpBlock\") (core/rule-kids ctx k)\n                               :else []))\n                           (core/kids ctx (p/root (:pk ctx))))\n        add (fn [st item] (-> st (update :items conj item) (assoc-in [:envs (:id item)] (:env st))))\n        ;; `namespace A;` parses as an expression statement over the constant\n        ;; `namespace A` (the grammar tries `statement` first)\n        stmt-ns (fn [head]\n                  (when (p/rule? head \"statement\")\n                    (let [es (first (core/rule-kids ctx head))\n                          e (when (p/rule? es \"expressionStatement\") (first (core/rules ctx es \"expression\")))\n                          c (when (and e (= 1 (count (core/kids ctx e)))) (first (core/rules ctx e \"constant\")))\n                          q (when (and c (= 1 (count (core/kids ctx c)))) (first (core/rules ctx c \"qualifiedNamespaceName\")))\n                          parts (when q (qname-parts ctx q))]\n                      (when (and parts (:ns-kw? parts) (not (:slash? parts)))\n                        (join-name (:segs parts))))))\n        step\n        (fn [st item]\n          (let [head (rule-head ctx item)\n                stmt-ns-name (stmt-ns head)]\n            (cond\n              (nil? head) (add st item)\n              (p/rule? head \"useDeclaration\") (update st :env #(apply-use ctx % head))\n              (or stmt-ns-name (p/rule? head \"namespaceDeclaration\"))\n              (let [nl (first (core/rules ctx head \"namespaceNameList\"))\n                    ns (cond stmt-ns-name stmt-ns-name\n                             nl (join-name (first (first (name-entries ctx nl []))))\n                             :else \"\")\n                    braced? (boolean (some #(and (p/token? %) (= \"{\" (:text %))) (core/kids ctx head)))\n                    form (if braced? :braced :unbraced)]\n                (when (:code-before? st)\n                  (compile-error! head \"Namespace declaration statement has to be the very first statement or after any declare call in the script\"))\n                (when (and (:form st) (not= form (:form st)))\n                  (compile-error! head \"Cannot mix bracketed namespace declarations with unbracketed namespace declarations\"))\n                (let [st (assoc st :form form :env {:ns ns, :uses (:uses global-env)})]\n                  (if braced?\n                    (let [st (reduce (fn [st s]\n                                       (let [h (first (core/rule-kids ctx s))]\n                                         (if (p/rule? h \"useDeclaration\")\n                                           (update st :env #(apply-use ctx % h))\n                                           (add st s))))\n                                     st\n                                     (core/rules ctx head \"namespaceStatement\"))]\n                      (assoc st :env global-env :after-braced? true))\n                    st)))\n              :else\n              (let [declare? (p/rule? (first (core/rule-kids ctx head)) \"declareStatement\")]\n                (when (and (:after-braced? st) (not declare?))\n                  (compile-error! head \"No code may exist outside of namespace {}\"))\n                (add (cond-> st\n                       (and (not (:form st)) (not declare?)) (assoc :code-before? true))\n                     item)))))]\n    (select-keys (reduce step {:items [], :envs {}, :env global-env} root-items) [:items :envs])))\n\n\n(defn- item-ctx\n  \"`ctx` carrying the namespace environment of top-level `item`.\"\n  [ctx item]\n  (merge ctx (get (:envs ctx) (:id item))))\n\n\n(defn- find-qname\n  \"The first `qualifiedNamespaceName` at or below `n`, in source order.\"\n  [ctx n]\n  (cond\n                    (remove #(or (contains? pnames %) (= \"$this\" %)))\n                    (mapv (fn [nm] {:name nm, :ref? false, :arrow? true})))\n               (mapv #(assoc % :arrow? false) (use-vars ctx n)))\n        caps (mapv #(assoc % :sym (symbol (str \"%cap\" (subs (:name %) 1) (:id n)))) caps)\n        _ (doseq [c caps] (checked-var n (:name c)))\n        static? (boolean (some #(and (p/token? %) (= \"Static\" (:type %))) (core/kids ctx n)))\n        [lam spec statics] (function-lam ctx n \"{closure}\" {:captures caps, :arrow? arrow?, :closure? true})\n        make (app* 'php/make-closure\n                   (app* 'php/closure-env\n                         (app* 'php/make-function (u/lit \"{closure}\") (u/lit spec) lam (u/lit statics))\n                         (if (and (:fn ctx) (not static?)) (app* 'php/this-or-nil (u/v '%fn)) (u/lit nil))\n                         (if (:fn ctx) (app* 'php/static-or-nil (u/v '%fn)) (u/lit nil))\n                         (cc-node ctx)))]\n    (reduce (fn [inner c] (u/let1 (:sym c) (capture-source ctx c) inner))\n            make\n            (reverse caps))))\n\n\n;; -----------------------------------------------------------------------------\n;; Objects and classes (P4 S1/S2)\n;; -----------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n(defn- line-of\n  \"The source line of CST node `n` from the packet's line side table, 0 when\n   the packet carries none.\"\n  [ctx n]\n  (let [starts (:yang.php/line-starts (:pk ctx))\n        at (first (:span n))]\n    (if (and (seq starts) at) (count (take-while #(<= % at) starts)) 0)))\n\n\n(defn- lower-new\n  \"`new Class(args)`: the class is resolved and refused first (row 53), the\n   object is created, then the arguments run, then the constructor.\"\n  [ctx n]\n  (let [t (first (core/rules ctx n \"typeRef\"))]\n\n(defn- class-item?\n  [ctx item]\n  (contains? #{\"classDeclaration\" \"enumDeclaration\"} (:rule (rule-head ctx item))))\n\n\n(defn- unit-body\n  \"The unit's statements as one node, hoisted function declarations first,\n   then the classes that can be declared at that point (PHP hoists a class\n   whose parent, interfaces and traits already exist); a hoisted class is\n   skipped when execution reaches it.\"\n  [ctx]\n  (let [items (:items ctx)\n        hoisted (filterv #(hoisted? ctx %) items)\n        classes (mapv (fn [item]\n                        (let [c (rule-head ctx item)\n                              [_ spec] (class-spec (item-ctx ctx item) c)]\n                          [(:id item) (symbol (str \"%class-\" (:id c))) spec]))\n                      (filter #(class-item? ctx %) items))\n        syms (into {} (map (fn [[id sym _]] [id sym])) classes)\n        in-place (fn [item]\n                   (if-let [sym (get syms (:id item))]\n                     (app* 'php/declare-late! (u/v sym))\n                     (lower (item-ctx ctx item) item)))]\n    (check-hoisted! ctx hoisted)\n    (let [body (sequence-node\n                 (concat (mapv #(lower (item-ctx ctx %) %) hoisted)\n                         (mapv (fn [[_ sym _]] (app* 'php/hoist-class! (u/v sym))) classes)\n                         (mapv in-place (remove #(hoisted? ctx %) items))))]\n      (reduce (fn [inner [_ sym spec]] (u/let1 sym (u/lam [] spec) inner))\n              body\n              (reverse classes)))))\n\n\n(defn- unit-returns?\n  \"True when the unit holds a top-level `return` (outside functions and\n   classes), which needs the escape around its body.\"\n  [ctx]\n  (core/contains-rule? ctx\n                       (p/root (:pk ctx))\n                       \"returnStatement\"\n                       #{\"functionDeclaration\" \"lambdaFunctionExpr\" \"classDeclaration\"\n                         \"enumDeclaration\"}))\n\n\n(defn- unit-node\n  \"`unit-body`, inside the `return` escape when the unit has a top-level\n   `return`: the escape answers its value, the sentinel `:php/no-return`\n   when the body falls off its end (plan P6 R4). An included unit's body\n   (`module?`) always answers the sentinel at its end; the entry unit's\n   value is dropped, so its tree is unchanged when it has no `return`.\"\n  ([ctx] (unit-node ctx false))\n  ([ctx module?]\n   (cond\n     (unit-returns? ctx)\n     (app* 'php/call-ec\n           (u/lam ['%ret] (u/then (unit-body (assoc ctx :ret '%ret)) (u/lit :php/no-return))))\n     module? (u/then (unit-body ctx) (u/lit :php/no-return))\n     :else (unit-body ctx))))\n\n\n\n(def ^:private builtins\n  \"The functions `php/init!` registers: PHP name to prelude definition,\n   derived from `builtins/supported`, the one table.\"\n  (mapv (fn [[nm {:keys [prelude]}]] [nm prelude]) (sort-by key builtins/supported)))\n\n\n(def builtin-names\n  \"The lower-cased names of the functions `php/init!` registers.\"\n  (set (map first builtins)))\n\n\n(def ^:private seed-classes\n  \"The builtin classes and interfaces `php/init!` seeds: [name kind parent\n   interfaces final?], parents before children (P4 owns the rest of the\n   builtin descriptor skeletons).\"\n                      (list 'php/int-lit (second v)))\n                    (and (vector? v) (= :float (first v)))\n                    (list 'php/f (list 'data/float-value (nth v 2)))\n                    :else v)))\n          {}\n          (sort-by key builtins/constants)))\n\n\n(defn- init-form\n  \"`php/init!`'s body: the runtime cells, the builtins, the ready flag, under\n   the uninit guard.\"\n  []\n  (list 'fn []\n        (list 'if (list '= 'php.rt/state :php/uninit)\n              (concat\n                ['do\n                 (define 'php.rt/ctx '(cell/new (php/ctx nil 0 0 nil)))\n                 (define 'php.rt/out '(cell/new [[]]))\n                 (define 'php.rt/request '(cell/new {}))\n                 (define 'php.rt/response '(cell/new []))\n                 (define 'php.rt/headers-sent '(cell/new false))\n                 (define 'php.rt/status '(cell/new 200))\n                 (define 'php.rt/error-handlers '(cell/new []))\n                 (define 'php.rt/globals\n                   '(cell/new (php/empty-array)))\n                 (define 'php.rt/functions '(cell/new {}))\n                 (define 'php.rt/classes (list 'cell/new seed-table))\n                 (define 'php.rt/class-index\n                   (list 'cell/new\n                         (into {} (map (fn [nm] [(str/lower-case nm) nm])) (keys seed-table))))\n                 (define 'php.rt/next-ord '(cell/new 1))\n                 (define 'php.rt/finalizable '(cell/new []))\n                 (define 'php.rt/strict '(cell/new false))\n                 (define 'php.rt/exception-handler '(cell/new :php/null))\n                 (define 'php.rt/exception-handlers '(cell/new []))\n                 (define 'php.rt/class-order '(cell/new []))\n                 (define 'php.rt/shutdown-fns '(cell/new []))\n                 (define 'php.rt/exit-status '(cell/new :php/null))\n                 (define 'php.rt/in-shutdown '(cell/new false))\n                 (define 'php.rt/fatal-escape '(cell/new :php/null))\n                 (define 'php.rt/exit-escape '(cell/new :php/null))\n                 (define 'php.rt/shutdown-escape '(cell/new :php/null))\n                 (define 'php.rt/pending-exc '(cell/new :php/null))\n                 (define 'php.rt/cmp-depth '(cell/new 0))\n                 (define 'php.rt/tmps '(cell/new []))\n                 (define 'php.rt/next-cell '(cell/new 1))\n                 (define 'php.rt/error-handler '(cell/new :php/null))\n                 (define 'php.rt/error-masks '(cell/new []))\n                 (define 'php.rt/error-mask '(cell/new 32767))\n                 ;; E_ALL\n                 (define 'php.rt/error-reporting '(cell/new 32767))\n                 (define 'php.rt/diag '(cell/new []))\n                 (define 'php.rt/response-stream '(cell/new :php/null))\n                 (define 'php.rt/diag-stream '(cell/new :php/null))\n                 (define 'php.rt/included '(cell/new {}))\n                 (define 'php.rt/unit '(cell/new :php/null))\n                 (define 'php.rt/path-map '(cell/new {}))\n                 (define 'php.rt/class-map '(cell/new {}))\n                 (define 'php.rt/autoloaders '(cell/new []))\n                 (define 'php.rt/autoloading '(cell/new {}))\n                 (define 'php.rt/int-max\n                   '(integer/sub (integer/shift-left 1 63) 1))\n                 (define 'php.rt/int-min\n                   '(integer/neg (integer/shift-left 1 63)))\n                 ;; after the integer bounds: the seeds build integers\n                 (define 'php.rt/constants (list 'cell/new (constants-form)))]\n                [(cons 'do\n                       (mapv (fn [[nm sym]] (list 'php/register! nm sym))\n                             builtins))]\n                ;; last, so a failed init never reports ready\n                [(define 'php.rt/state :php/ready) :php/null])\n              :php/null)))\n\n\n(def definitions\n  \"The single definition list, `[store-key form]` in definition order: every\nsrc/cljc/yang/core/publication.cljc:15:   `:site-set`          `(fn [handle address ast])` -> site publication, or nil\nsrc/cljc/yang/core/publication.cljc:104:  (let [{:keys [imported-names module-spec scc-module-specs site-set\nsrc/cljc/yang/core/publication.cljc:138:                                    (emit1 :sites site-set)\nsrc/cljc/yang/core/publication.cljc:142:                                  (refused (keyword refusal-ns \"site-set-unpublished\")\nsrc/cljc/yang/python/antlr/siteset.cljc:8:   sorted (`yang.safepoint/site-set`) and content-addressed. A separate\nsrc/cljc/yang/python/antlr/siteset.cljc:62:  :yang.python.antlr/site-set)\nsrc/cljc/yang/python/antlr/siteset.cljc:65:(defn site-set-of\nsrc/cljc/yang/python/antlr/siteset.cljc:71:                               (medium) [:site-set 0] [ast]))\nsrc/cljc/yang/python/antlr/siteset.cljc:76:    {:root (:root tree), :tree tree, :set (safepoint/site-set sites)}))\nsrc/cljc/yang/python/antlr/siteset.cljc:95:  (let [{:keys [root set]} (site-set-of ast)\nsrc/cljc/yang/python/antlr/siteset.cljc:275:      (refusal :yang.python.antlr/missing-site-set requirement\nsrc/cljc/yang/python/antlr/siteset.cljc:294:            (refusal :yang.python.antlr/site-set-mismatch requirement\nsrc/cljc/yang/python/antlr/siteset.cljc:496:  #{:yang.python.antlr/missing-site-set\nsrc/cljc/yang/python/antlr/siteset.cljc:497:    :yang.python.antlr/site-set-mismatch\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
